# Benchy — UI Guidelines

Full reference: `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`. Homepage (`src/shell/home.css`) is the visual north star.

## Consistency

- Maintain the existing design language (`--lt-*` tokens in `src/shared/theme.css`).
- Reuse `ToolHeader`, `LtTabs`, `ToolActionBar`, `lt-btn`, `lt-input` — do not invent new button/tab/header systems.
- Preserve existing UX patterns: workspace Save/Import/Export in shell top bar; tool exports in `ToolActionBar`.

## Layout density

- Tool header ~40px; tabs single row; action bar single row.
- Sidebars are for tool configuration only — not global project navigation.
- Primary data (gels, charts, images) gets remaining flex space.

## Tool CSS

- Scope styles under a root class (e.g. `.qpcr-insight`, `.gq-*`).
- Avoid global `.btn` / unscoped leaks.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Adding UI for a new tool

1. `.app` flex column inside the shell tab panel
2. `ToolHeader` + optional `LtTabs` + `ToolActionBar`
3. Register in shell manifests
4. Wire persistence snapshot
